# Pure or not? Sorting what you know

Now that you've seen how each method behaves, let's look at the bigger picture.

Pure functions and side effects aren't just about individual methods,they reflect 
two different approaches to working with data. 

Understanding the difference will help you write code that is easier to predict, test, and share with others.


## Pure Function vs. Side Effects

<div style="display:flex; gap:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; margin-top:16px;">

  <div style="background:#f0eefa; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; width:360px;">
    <strong style="font-size:14pt; color:#444;">Pure function</strong>
    <ul>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Predictable results</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Original data stays the same</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Easier to test and debug</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Safer for shared data</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="background:#f0f0ee; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; width:360px;">
    <strong style="font-size:14pt; color:#444;">Function with side effects</strong>
    <ul>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Can change data unexpectedly</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Harder to reason about</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Order of operations matters</li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Can impact other code</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>

### **Common Methods and Their Behavior**

<div style="display:flex; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; margin-top:16px;">

  <div style="background:#f0eefa; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; width:360px;">
    <strong style="font-size:14pt; color:#444;">Pure (non-mutating)</strong>
    <p style="font-size:14pt;">These methods return a <strong>new array</strong> and leave the original unchanged.</p>
    <ul>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><code>.map()</code></li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><code>.filter()</code></li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Loops that build a copy</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="background:#f0f0ee; border-radius:12px; padding:14px; width:360px;">
    <strong style="font-size:14pt; color:#444;">Mutating (side effects)</strong>
    <p style="font-size:14pt;">These approaches can change existing data or rely on external effects.</p>
    <ul>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><code>.forEach()</code></li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;"><code>.shift()</code></li>
      <li style="font-size:14pt;">Loops that modify the original array</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>

---

